# Blade of the Swarm's "put target exiled card with warp on the bottom of its owner's library": the target is any card in
# exile that has warp, not only one warp exiled (the ruling). Bot2 casts Bygone Colossus for its warp cost and Bot1 exiles it
# with Swords to Plowshares before the end step, so warp's own exile finds nothing (it is a new object, CR 400.7). Memnite,
# which Bot1 exiled with Swords on turn 1, has no warp and is no target, so the Colossus is the one legal target and is
# taken without a prompt. It goes to the bottom of Bot2's library, its owner's, not Bot1's, and Memnite stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Swords to Plowshares
Swords to Plowshares
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Blade of the Swarm
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mana Crypt
Blasted Landscape
Bygone Colossus
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Blasted Landscape.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Blasted Landscape.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Bygone Colossus.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Bygone Colossus)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Exile.Bygone Colossus.Power = 9
? Exile = Memnite; Bygone Colossus
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Blade of the Swarm.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Put target exiled card)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile = Memnite
Bot2.Library = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island; Bygone Colossus
Bot1.Battlefield.Blade of the Swarm.Power = 3
Bot2.Life = 29
